  "summary_en": "European Parliament resolution of 20 January 2021 on AI and international law, covering military uses, state authority, justice, health and transport. It calls for a common EU legal framework, meaningful human control, a ban on lethal autonomous weapons without human control, and international negotiations on military AI.",
  "title_clean": "Artificial intelligence: questions of interpretation and application of international law",
  "title_en": "Artificial intelligence: questions of interpretation and application of international law",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Calls for a common European legal framework with harmonised AI definitions and ethical principles, including for military AI.",
   "Requires meaningful human control over military and civil AI, with the ability to correct, halt or disable it.",
   "Insists on an EU-wide strategy against LAWS and a ban on systems without human control.",
   "Urges global negotiations on an AI arms control regime and a legally binding CCW instrument on LAWS.",
   "Asks for safeguards, impact assessments and human review in AI used by public authorities and in justice, and a possible facial recognition moratorium."
  ],
